{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "General Indemnities in Software License Agreements"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear regarding indemnities in license agreements"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Participates in the improvement of IT contracts, establishing technical clauses that respond to the needs of the negotiating agents, based on current laws on contracting."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "burden "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "any action that results in a restrictive load on something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You, as the customer, are supposed to understand the burdens and benefits of general indemnities provisions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fault "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "deficiency that can cause the failure of a component or system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This allocation can be based on fault, which means the risk is allocated to the contracting party whose acts or omissions regarding the software caused the third party claim. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "indemnity "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "legal compensation for injury, loss or damage"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The main purpose of a general indemnity is to contractually allocate the risk of claims by, as I said, third parties against the contracting parties."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "liability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "claim against the legal obligations of an organization or person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An obligation to reimburse and protect the beneficiary from obligations and liabilities resulting from those claims."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "party "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "entity that takes part in a legal agreement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Efficiency, in which case the risk is allocated to the contracting party who is best to manage the third party claim.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reimburse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pay back; to refund"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An obligation to reimburse and protect the beneficiary from obligations and liabilities resulting from those claims."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "a) Look for information about General Indemnities in Software License Agreements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "b) Describe IP Infringement Indemnity and Remedies included in a licensed software."}, {"type": "text", "content": "c) Write a text of 300 words in which you explain its relevance and the type of remedies a customer can get."}, {"type": "text", "content": "d) Share your text with your instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI look for information about general indemnities in the software license agreement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI describe the indemnities and remedies customers can get."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI write an IP infringement indemnity model ."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI share the document with my classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed To and Simple Present Passive Voice to Talk About Technology Negotiation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When people discuss the terms included in an IT procurement or contract, the grammar forms <span class =\"strong\"> be supposed to  </span> and <span class =\"strong\"> the passive voice of the simple present  </span> are commonly used."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\"> Be supposed to  </span> in its present form is used to say that something is expected to happen or that someone is obliged to do it: <br/><br/> Subject + <span class =\"strong\"> be (am/is/are) + supposed to </span> + verb base form + complement <br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"> \u2022 Contracts <span class =\"strong\"> are supposed to include </span> indemnities to protect customers. </span> <br/><br/> The <span class =\"strong\"> simple present in the passive voice  </span> is used to talk about situations that are expected to occur on a regular basis and whose doer is unknown or is not important.  <br/><br/> Review the following structure: <br/><br/> <span class =\"strong\"> Object + to be verb + main verb (past participle) + complement </span> <br/><br/> Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> \u2022 The risk <span class =\"strong\"> is allocated </span> to the beneficiary party. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you probably know, indemnities are supposed to impose obligations on the parties in case there is a claim by a third party."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You, as the customer, are supposed to understand the burdens and benefits of general indemnities provisions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The risk is allocated to the contracting party whose acts or omissions regarding the software caused the third party claim."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The scope of a general indemnity is adjusted according to who the beneficiaries are supposed to be."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class =\"strong\"> Phrasal verbs  </span> are two-word verbs made out of a verb and a preposition. Their meaning is not easy to identify at first glance."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some <span class =\"strong\"> phrasal verbs  </span> cannot be separated, and they always go together no matter what the object is. Here is a list of the most common <span class =\"strong\"> inseparable phrasal verbs</span>:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":14,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrasal verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Catch up </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To become equal or reach the same level\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Come across </span>\\\